{"name":"Bakery Box","hex":"#f0f4f2","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bakery","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A place in which bread (and often other baked goods such as cakes) is baked and/or sold.","The trade of a baker."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bakery"},{"term":"box","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Buamu."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Senses relating to a three-dimensional object or space.\n A cuboid space; a cuboid container, often with a hinged lid.","A cuboid space; a cuboid container, often with a hinged lid."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/box"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bakery","blocks":[{"text":"A bakery is an establishment that produces and sells flour-based baked goods made in an oven such as bread, cookies, cakes, doughnuts, pizzas, bagels, pastries, and pies. Some retail bakeries are also categorized as cafés, serving coffee and tea to customers who wish to consume the baked goods on the premises. In some countries, a distinction is made between bakeries, which primarily sell breads, and pâtisseries, which primarily sell sweet baked goods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Belgium_2013_%2811620905224%29.jpg/330px-Belgium_2013_%2811620905224%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bakery","wikidata":"Q274393"},{"title":"Box","blocks":[{"text":"A box is a container with rigid sides used for the storage or transportation of its contents. Most boxes have flat, parallel, rectangular sides. Boxes can be very small or very large and can be used for a variety of purposes, from functional to decorative."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/L%C3%A5da_-_Livrustkammaren_-_107142.tif/lossy-page1-330px-L%C3%A5da_-_Livrustkammaren_-_107142.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=t